Article 11 protects freedom of peaceful assembly. It includes both negative obligations (not to interfere) and positive obligations (to ensure effective exercise, protect against third-party violence, investigate violations). The Court has recognized positive obligations regarding protection of participants from violence by private persons and sometimes police.

